.TH MORSECODE 1
.SH NAME
morsecode \- a straight key you tap
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/morsecode
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I MorseCode
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Snd/MorseCode.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
The whole decoder is two numbers.  A key held for under a hundred and
forty milliseconds is a dot and longer is a dash; a gap of three hundred
milliseconds or more ends the letter.  Nothing is calibrated to your
speed and nothing adapts.  A tone sounds while the key is down and stops
on release, as a real straight key does.
.PP
Above the key is the whole International Morse alphabet \- letters,
digits and punctuation \- in four columns of thirteen, as the original
prints it.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Tap to send
.TP
.B Esc / q
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/morsecode.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR tone (2),
.IR wm (1)
